WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.379
Text Structure and Purpose

00:00:02.759 --> 00:00:04.526
Ask what the author is DOING.

00:00:05.726 --> 00:00:06.817
How to spot it

00:00:07.217 --> 00:00:10.814
The question says “main purpose” or “overall structure”

00:00:11.364 --> 00:00:13.229
Or one underlined sentence

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:17.568
It’s testing: the job each part of a text is doing

00:00:18.768 --> 00:00:19.534
The method

00:00:19.934 --> 00:00:23.247
Step 1: Label each sentence with a verb

00:00:23.527 --> 00:00:26.691
introduces, describes, challenges, concludes

00:00:27.241 --> 00:00:30.439
Step 2: Purpose = the main action

00:00:30.719 --> 00:00:32.660
One verb for the whole text.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:36.759
Step 3: Structure = the actions in order

00:00:37.039 --> 00:00:39.236
Belief, then evidence against it.

00:00:39.786 --> 00:00:42.325
Step 4: Check every word

00:00:42.605 --> 00:00:44.610
One wrong verb kills the choice.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.255
In a few words

00:00:46.405 --> 00:00:49.672
Label. Combine. Check every word.

00:00:50.872 --> 00:00:51.680
Verb check

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.562
Describe ≠ argue

00:00:53.842 --> 00:00:55.748
Informing is not persuading.

00:00:56.298 --> 00:00:58.013
Question ≠ refute

00:00:58.293 --> 00:00:59.997
Doubting is not disproving.

00:01:00.547 --> 00:01:02.120
Function, not content

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.857
What the sentence does, not what it says.

00:01:05.407 --> 00:01:06.657
Two-part answers

00:01:06.937 --> 00:01:08.589
Both halves must be right.

00:01:09.789 --> 00:01:10.850
Let’s try one

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:16.028
Many people believe that goldfish have a memory span of only a few seconds.

00:01:16.028 --> 00:01:18.515
Experiments tell a different story.

00:01:18.515 --> 00:01:23.937
In one study, goldfish were trained to push a lever for food at a particular time of day;

00:01:23.937 --> 00:01:27.483
months later, they still approached the lever at that hour.

00:01:27.483 --> 00:01:32.508
Such results suggest that goldfish memory is far more durable than commonly assumed.

00:01:33.058 --> 00:01:36.777
Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?

00:01:37.427 --> 00:01:40.829
Label each sentence. First, a common belief.

00:01:41.379 --> 00:01:43.205
Then, evidence against it.

00:01:43.755 --> 00:01:45.090
Then, a conclusion.

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:50.124
Belief, evidence, conclusion. Only B has all three, in order.

00:01:51.324 --> 00:01:52.393
Common traps

00:01:52.793 --> 00:01:53.546
Wrong verb

00:01:53.826 --> 00:01:56.618
“Argues” when the author only describes.

00:01:57.168 --> 00:01:57.904
Half right

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:00.298
First part right, second part wrong.

00:02:01.498 --> 00:02:03.276
Text Structure and Purpose

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:06.824
Label. Combine. Check every word.

00:02:07.374 --> 00:02:07.954
Spot it

00:02:08.154 --> 00:02:12.938
“main purpose”, “overall structure”, or an underlined sentence

00:02:13.488 --> 00:02:14.195
Steps

00:02:14.395 --> 00:02:16.677
1. Label each sentence with a verb

00:02:16.957 --> 00:02:19.049
2. Purpose = the main action

00:02:19.329 --> 00:02:21.772
3. Structure = the actions in order

00:02:22.052 --> 00:02:24.141
4. Check every word of the choice

00:02:24.691 --> 00:02:25.416
Remember

00:02:25.616 --> 00:02:27.166
describe ≠ argue

00:02:27.446 --> 00:02:29.138
question ≠ refute

00:02:29.418 --> 00:02:32.129
Function = what it does, not what it says

00:02:32.409 --> 00:02:34.702
Two-part answers: both halves right

00:02:35.252 --> 00:02:35.693
Trap

00:02:35.893 --> 00:02:38.685
“Argues” when the author only describes

00:02:39.435 --> 00:02:42.853
